      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/97f17d/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-05T01:32:03.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm looking for an official ruling. &nbsp;Meteor Storm is in play (\"At the start of their turn, a hero may skip the rest of their turn to destroy this card). Scholar has an elemental form in play and wishes to destroy Meteor Storm, &nbsp;For his first start of turn action he skips the rest of his turn and destroys Meter Storm. &nbsp;Having had some segment of a start of turn, but ending before paying upkeep on the form, does he loose his form? &nbsp;Or does he skip that requirement by skipping during start?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:57.584Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 5.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 11613,
      "topic_slug": "meteor-storm-and-start-of-turn-upkeep-cost",
      "display_username": "DrScott",
      "primary_group_name": null,
