      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I&#39;m looking for an official ruling. &nbsp;Meteor Storm is in play (&quot;At the start of their turn, a hero may skip the rest of their turn to destroy this card). Scholar has an elemental form in play and wishes to destroy Meteor Storm, &nbsp;For his first start of turn action he skips the rest of his turn and destroys Meter Storm. &nbsp;Having had some segment of a start of turn, but ending before paying upkeep on the form, does he loose his form? &nbsp;Or does he skip that requirement by skipping during start?</p>",
