    {
      "id": 121782,
      "name": "phantaskippy",
      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-12-05T01:43:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It would depend on which came into play first. &nbsp;If the form was in play first its start of turn occurs first, and you would have to pay the cost before having the option of skipping to destroy Meteor Storm.</p><p>If Meteor Storm entered play first, it would resolve first and the requirements for the form would be skipped, since as far as that card is concerned the start of your turn never happened.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>EDIT: &nbsp;As soon as the phone rang I thought, \"I bet Ronway answers while I'm on the phone.\" &nbsp;Yeah.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:55:24.800Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
